/-!
Source/core/bridge triage for this item.

- `source-facing`: Corollary 13.2.1 identifies the closure `cl(f)` of a positively homogeneous
  convex function with the support function of the explicit set `{x⋆ | ∀ x, ⟪x, x⋆⟫ₚ ≤ f x}`.
- `core/canonical`: the owner declarations already present in the project are
  `cl(·)`, `δᵛ(· | ·)`, `f⋆`, `Function.sublinearHull`,
  `Function.PositivelyHomogeneous`, `ConvexOn` on `Set.univ`, and `f.IsProper`.
- `bridge/view`: the displayed set `{x⋆ | ∀ x, ⟪x, x⋆⟫ₚ ≤ f x}` is treated as the source-facing
  description of the canonical owner set `{x⋆ | f⋆ x⋆ ≤ 0}`.

Primitive data vs derived API:
- primitive inputs: the function `f` together with its positive homogeneity, convexity, and
  properness hypotheses;
- derived API: the bridge from the canonical nonpositive conjugate sublevel set to the textbook
  set-builder, and the source-facing support-function formula for `cl(f)`.

Layer target: `source-facing`; the item keeps Rockafellar's explicit support set, but its main
identity is governed by the owner-side generated-hull API rather than by a parallel local wrapper.

Abstraction audit for this file:
- codomain layer: the bridge from `f⋆ x⋆ ≤ 0` to the pointwise pairing inequalities lives at the
  `WithTopBot α` codomain layer (for ordered additive `α`) rather than at the concrete alias
  `EReal = WithTopBot ℝ`;
- scalar/pairing layer: the Corollary 13.2.1 closure/support-function statements below are stated
  on a finite-dimensional module `X` over an ordered scalar field `𝕜`, paired with a dual-side
  space `Y`; no inner-product self-pairing specialization is built into the public owner surface;
- topology criterion: this corollary is function-side (`cl(f)` as lower-semicontinuous hull), not a
  set-side ambient-vs-relative topology statement (`closure`/`intrinsicClosure` on subsets), so the
  intrinsic-topology replacement criterion is inapplicable for this item.

Domain-style sampling used here:
- `cl(·)`;
- `δᵛ(· | ·)`;
- direct unfolding of `f⋆`;
- `Function.isGreatest_sublinearHull_minorant`;
- the chapter generated-hull support-function identity behind Corollary 13.2.1.
-/

-- Proof sketch: unfold `f⋆ xStar`; the inequality `f⋆ xStar ≤ 0` means every affine defect
-- `⟪x, xStar⟫ₚ - f x` is nonpositive, which is equivalent to `⟪x, xStar⟫ₚ ≤ f x` for all `x`.
/-- The canonical nonpositive sublevel set of `f⋆` is exactly the textbook set
`{x⋆ | ∀ x, ⟪x, x⋆⟫ₚ ≤ f x}`. This bridge uses only the pairing owner layer and therefore does
not require an inner-product-space ambient model. -/
theorem nonpositiveSublevel_convexConjugate_eq_setOf_forall_pairing_le
    (f : X → WithTopBot α) :
    {y : Y | f⋆ y ≤ 0} =
      {y : Y | ∀ x : X, ⟪x, y⟫ₚ ≤ f x} := by
  ext y
  simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq]
  rw [convexConjugate_eq_iSup_pairing_sub, iSup_le_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h x
    exact sub_nonpos.mp (h x)
  · intro h x
    exact sub_nonpos.mpr (h x)

end

